  f050: { lead: '1348 — the Black Death arrives. It is the single biggest demographic event in British history, and it happens in the middle of the Hundred Years War.' },
  f051: { lead: 'About a third of the population died. The labour shortage that followed gave surviving peasants bargaining power, which began the end of the feudal system — the consequence matters more than the number.' },
